*$py.class
*.so
.Python
env/
build/
develop-eggs/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
# Anchored to the repo root. These come from the standard Python template,
# where they mean a virtualenv's internals -- but unanchored they match ANY
# directory of that name at any depth, and `lib/` was silently swallowing
# frontend/src/lib/ (api.js, supabase.js, voice.js). Those are load-bearing:
# every page imports from them, so a fresh clone would not even build. The
# venv dirs themselves are already ignored wholesale further down.
/lib/
/lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
venv/
.venv/
venv.bak/

# Prisma
backend/prisma/schema/*.db
.fastembed_cache/
backend/.fastembed_cache/

